      "answer": "$4e^{-1}=\\frac4e$.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "Commence integration and reach $a(2-x)e^{-x/2}+b\\int e^{-x/2}\\,dx$ — *M1, condoning omission of $dx$; e.g. $-2(2-x)e^{-x/2}-4e^{-x/2}$ or $2xe^{-x/2}$.\n\nObtain $-2(2-x)e^{-x/2}-2\\int e^{-x/2}\\,dx$ — A1, OE.\n\nComplete the integration and obtain $2xe^{-x/2}$ — A1, OE.\n\nUse the correct limits $x=0$ and $x=2$, correctly, having integrated twice — DM1. Ignore omission of zeros and allow a maximum of one error.\n\nObtain $4e^{-1}$, or exact equivalent — A1, ISW.\n\nAlternative method: differentiate $2xe^{-x/2}$ to obtain $2e^{-x/2}-xe^{-x/2}$ — *M1 A1; hence use the antiderivative $2xe^{-x/2}$ — A1; use the correct limits $0$ and $2$ — DM1 with the same guidance; obtain $4e^{-1}$ — A1, ISW.\n\nTotal [5].",
